WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
You rush into a cinema.

2
00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.860
You're late. Maybe you sit down,

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.650
and then the film starts.

4
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.550
Or maybe it started without you,

5
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.260
and you missed the opening.

6
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.090
Later, a French friend asks how it went.

7
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.000
You begin: «Quand je suis arrivé,

8
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.240
le film…» And you stop.

9
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.080
Two different stories, and your
next words have to pick one.

10
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.360
So how does French show that one
past event happened before another?

11
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.130
In this mission, you'll place events
on Mission D1's two-past timeline.

12
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.580
Then you'll follow Lucas
on his trip to Paris

13
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.710
in Mission I1 and put his day in order.

14
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: work out how French
puts one past event before another.
